  "final_message": "I've built the weather display: a Flask API backed by SQLite, and a React + TypeScript + Tailwind frontend served by the same app. I tested the API by running it locally under gunicorn with a script, and every endpoint returned the expected status and body. The frontend type-checks and builds, but I never opened it in a browser. I also couldn't build or run the Docker image (Docker isn't available here), so that path is untested.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- **Seed data:** on first start the database at `data/app.db` gets eight sample cities. They are added only once and survive restarts.\n- **Accounts:** login returns a token that lasts 7 days. Adding, replacing and deleting reports need that token; without a valid one they answer 401.\n- **Reads are public:** listing reports, fetching one, and recent lookups need no sign-in.\n- **Lookups:** a `city` search matches whole names ignoring case, and records the lookup with whether it was found. An empty `city` is treated as a plain list and isn't recorded. Recent lookups default to 5.\n- **Errors:** bad input answers 400 with an overall message plus a message per field. A duplicate city or username answers 409, and a missing report answers 404.\n- **Paging:** `page_size` defaults to 10. Values above 100 are reduced to 100 rather than rejected.\n- **Unrequested additions:** I added `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` so the frontend can check a saved sign-in and sign out properly.\n\n**Validation limits I chose** (the spec didn't give any):\n- City is required, up to 100 characters.\n- Temperature is required, between \u2212100 and 70 \u00b0C.\n- Humidity must be 0\u2013100.\n- Wind must be 0\u2013500 km/h.\n- Username must be 3\u201350 characters and password 4\u2013200.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src/App.tsx`, `frontend/src/api.ts`)\n- Sign-in and registration forms; once signed in, the header shows the username and a sign-out button.\n- City search shows the weather card or \"No weather data for <city>\".\n- The \u00b0C/\u00b0F switch converts temperatures in the browser.\n- The five most recent lookups are listed, and clicking one repeats the search.\n- Signed-in users get the paged report list with add and edit forms that show the API's messages, and delete asks for confirmation first.\n- Styling is Tailwind only; `src/index.css` contains just the Tailwind import.\n\n**Other changes**\n- `npm run build` now type-checks before building, and there is a new `npm run typecheck`. The new dependencies are pinned in `package-lock.json`.\n- I added a `.gitignore` and a short section to `README.md`.\n\nThe Python lock file wouldn't install with the older pip in this sandbox, but it installs fine with pip 26, which the Docker image should use.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
